omprising juice, milk, and wine; and custom sheeting and slitting of paperboard products. It serves packaging converters through sales managers. The company was founded in 1926 and is headquartered in Spokane, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Arsen S. Kitch | CEO, President & Director | Age 43 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $819K ranks in the above the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Clearwater Paper Corporation is a micro-cap basic materials business with a $286M market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $76M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 488% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.881515990934274},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 82/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 79% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Basic Materials sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Charter Hall Long WALE REIT (ASX:CLW): Is the ASX 200 Property and Infrastructure Name's Rental Income Base Gathering Momentum?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/charter-hall-long-wale-reit-asxclw-is-the-asx-200-property-and-infrastructure-names-rental-income-base-gathering-momentum","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795756380.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[